From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 12:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: camss: keep sm8150 DMA inside the addressable range

The vendor device tree restricts the IFE context bank's IOVA region to
0x07400000 through 0xe0000000. Linux allocates from the top of the 32-bit
space, so buffers land at 0xff000000 and above, outside it.

On this SoC the write master then reports its transfer complete while issuing
no memory write at all: buffers queued pre-filled with a known pattern come
back with the pattern untouched, while the CSID byte counter shows a full frame
handed over every frame.

Narrow the mask so allocations stay inside the range the hardware is described
as addressing.

Signed-off-by: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -4019,7 +4019,18 @@
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto err_genpd_cleanup;
 
-	ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, 0xffffffff);
+	/*
+	 * The vendor device tree restricts the IFE context bank's IOVA region
+	 * to 0x07400000..0xe0000000. Linux allocates from the top of the 32-bit
+	 * space, which lands at 0xff000000 and above, outside it. On SM8150 the
+	 * write master then reports its transfer done without issuing a single
+	 * memory write, so keep allocations inside the range the hardware is
+	 * described as addressing.
+	 */
+	if (camss->res->version == CAMSS_8150)
+		ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(31));
+	else
+		ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, 0xffffffff);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_genpd_cleanup;
 
--
2.50.1
